    {
      "id": "sticky_overview",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -60,
        -600
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 1040,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## 🦷 Dental Lead Nurturing & Appointment Automation\n\nThis template contains **two independent flows**, each starting from its own webhook:\n\n**1️⃣ Lead Nurture Flow** (top row) — captures a new lead, sends an instant welcome, then checks in at 1hr → Day 1 → Day 3 → Day 7 until the lead books or is marked lost.\n\n**2️⃣ Appointment Flow** (bottom row) — triggered once a lead books. Creates the calendar event, then sends 24hr and 2hr reminders, followed by a post-visit review request.\n\n**Before activating:**\n- Connect your Google Sheets, Twilio, Gmail and Google Calendar credentials\n- Create a Google Sheet named \"Leads\" with columns: Name, Phone, Email, Service, Source, Status, CreatedAt, AppointmentDateTime\n- Replace all [bracketed] placeholders (clinic name, booking link, address, review link)\n- Point your lead form / booking system at the two webhook URLs"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky_phase1",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -60,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 740,
        "height": 220,
        "content": "### Phase 1 — Capture & Log Lead\nA new lead (website form, Meta/Google Lead Ads, chatbot, etc.) hits this webhook. We normalize the fields into consistent variables, log the lead into a Google Sheet (acting as a lightweight CRM), then check whether a phone number was provided."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky_phase2",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        860,
